msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:171
#: df82517a9f59403abae598f8b2060d70
msgid "If you are on Windows then download and install MAVProxy from https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/MAVProxy/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:174
#: 82e6c701582e4aa7810049b98c6c6edb
msgid "Then do a git checkout of ArduPilot master and change directory to the ArduPlane directory. I like to create a sub-directory for each aircraft I fly in SITL so that settings are remembered per-aircraft. If you want to do that then create a subdirectory in the ArduPlane directory and run sim_vehicle.py from there. In the following example I will be using the PT60 aircraft in X-Plane, so I create a PT60 directory::"
msgstr ""

