#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:219
#: 3bd24a9769564a2199908a5d2c841ee0
msgid "Flying a Helicopter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:221
#: ae1167df6d8845719bef3837bb3b1de3
msgid "It is also possible to fly a helicopter with XPlane-10/11. The setup is similar to a plane, with two additional requirements:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:224
#: 9fc93908e7fe4e8d906783a7cad5aafd
msgid "you need to setup your XPlane joystick to map the collective stick to flaps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:226
#: 257db2747cdf48b0a1e52e7c88065241
msgid "you need to map a key or joystick button to turn on and off the \"generator1\" electrical system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:229
#: 3a1b7a1c52384a89bf3fc08753a435b1
msgid "These strange requirements are because of limitations in the remote control of helicopters in X-Plane 10. The flaps input is something that ArduPilot SITL is able to read remotely while not interfering with flight of the helicopter. The \"generator1 on/off\" is used to simulate the interlock switch (channel 8) in ArduPilot helicopter support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:236
#: 35176f012a474982a4b0a9b4efc13cb5
msgid "Note that for \"generator on/off\" you do need to map two separate events, one for on and one for off. If using a two position switch then map one to the switch on position and the other to the switch off position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:241
#: aedd369ae36a414ead03099646c0e479
msgid "See this example for typical joystick setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:246
#: 771eb19cd03c44b48cde7e5c788c7748
msgid "and this one for mapping the generator on/off switch to a joystick switch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:252
#: 2acc30500131468cb674ff842923d0ae
msgid "A full set of parameters for the Bell JetRanger Helicopter in X-Plane 10/11 are available here http://uav.tridgell.net/XPlane/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:255
#: 777afd2d76a043be9aace34db44c3196
msgid "You also need to start SITL with the model set to \"xplane-heli\" instead of \"xplane\" to activate Helicopter controls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:258
#: 1e845cd7211c45c39bde6b6567bb9e96
msgid "The startup procedure for a helicopter is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:260
#: f79253ea08c04fea946a25676a084b74
msgid "set interlock on (so RC input channel 8 is low)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:261
#: 87c184ba03f24ca8a8446e391d395d55
msgid "set zero collective (so RC input channel 3 is low)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:262
#: eeac1b9beae0415b8001a559e8512df6
msgid "arm the helicopter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:263
#: d28650bf3d1543e7934eb46aa4a3b9e8
msgid "set interlock off (so RC input channel 8 is high)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:264
#: 72102a6e25a341f68dfc4e4b091bb958
msgid "wait for the head to reach full speed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-xplane.rst:265
#: da398496cac646029946ca514e0957e4
msgid "takeoff"
msgstr ""
